    <suppress until="2026-12-29Z">
        <notes><![CDATA[
        Reviewed 2026-09-30: Elasticsearch server CVEs incorrectly matched to the
        Java API client and low-level HTTP REST client, version 9.1.2 only.
        ElasticsearchClientFactory uses RestClientTransport to call an external
        cluster; these two client artifacts do not implement the server's search
        aggregation or index analysis execution. This does not suppress findings
        against org.elasticsearch:elasticsearch or its server modules, and does
        not establish that the separately deployed Elasticsearch cluster is safe.
        Review again on dependency or architecture changes, or before expiry.

        Client architecture: https://www.elastic.co/docs/reference/elasticsearch/clients/java
        CVE-2026-82294: https://discuss.elastic.co/t/390681
        CVE-2026-82300: https://discuss.elastic.co/t/390682
        CVE-2026-94398: https://discuss.elastic.co/t/390683
        CVE-2026-94399: https://discuss.elastic.co/t/390684
        CVE-2026-94397: https://discuss.elastic.co/t/390687
        ]]></notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/(co\.elastic\.clients/elasticsearch-java|org\.elasticsearch\.client/elasticsearch-rest-client)@9\.1\.2$</packageUrl>
        <cve>CVE-2026-82294</cve>
